== the outer list breaks and the inner stays packed
faithful: true, fixpoint
1 |x = outer_call(|
2 |    inner_call(a, b),|
3 |    second_argument,|
4 |    third_argument,|
5 |    fourth_argument|
6 |)|
== the same two lists on one line come out the same way
faithful: true, fixpoint
1 |x = outer_call(|
2 |    inner_call(a, b),|
3 |    second_argument,|
4 |    third_argument,|
5 |    fourth_argument|
6 |)|
== a hand-wrapped list that fits is packed back onto one line
faithful: true, fixpoint
1 |x = outer_call(inner_call(a, b), second_argument)|
== an operator chain of calls is a human's to re-shape
faithful: true, fixpoint
1 |r = kind.same(TokenKind.BraceOpen) || kind.same(TokenKind.ParenOpen) || kind.ret_start()|
